schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Wyoming DUNA requires 100+ members and on-chain governance
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    The Wyoming Decentralized Unincorporated Nonprofit Association (DUNA),
    effective July 1, 2024, gives DAO members liability protection (a
    judgment against the DUNA does not reach individuals) but the statute
    requires at least 100 members plus meaningful on-chain governance,
    making it suitable for a maturing node, not a five-person start.
  evidence: >-
    Cited to "Global Fintech & Digital Assets Blog, Wyoming Adopts New Legal
    Structure for DAOs" (2024) for the effective date and 100-member rule,
    and to "a16z crypto, The DUNA: An Oasis for DAOs" for the liability-
    shield mechanics; the Uniswap Foundation's DUNI (established via
    governance vote in 2025) is cited as a worked real-world adopter.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/legal-structures.md
  interpretation: >-
    High-risk/governance claim: accurately reflects what the article's cited
    sources say, but a DAO considering this structure should verify current
    statute text directly (Wyoming Secretary of State) rather than relying
    on secondary summaries, since the structure is new (2024) and still
    accumulating case law and administrative practice.
  uncertainty: >-
    Moderate — sourced to named secondary articles (Global Fintech & Digital
    Assets Blog, a16z) rather than the statute text itself; the 100-member
    threshold and its practical enforcement are asserted, not independently
    verified against the current Wyoming statute in this ingest pass.
  high_risk: true
  maturity: raw
  public_use: requires-domain-review
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/legal-structures.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
